"ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "sequenceIndex": 5, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadith VI", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "sequenceIndex": 6, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَمْرٍو رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ ذَكَرَ الصَّلَاةَ يَوْمًا فَقَالَ مَنْ حَافَظَ عَلَيْهَا كَانَتْ لَهُ نُورًا وَبُرْهَانًا وَنَجَاةً يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَمَنْ لَمْ يُحَافِظْ عَلَيْهَا لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهُ نُورٌ وَلَا بُرْهَانٌ وَلَا نَجَاةٌ وَكَانَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ مَعَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامَانَ وَقَارُونَ وَأُبَيِّ بْنِ خَلَفٍ", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "sequenceIndex": 7, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "أخرجه أحمد وابن حبان", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "sequenceIndex": 8, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Abdullah bin Amr (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that once the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) while talking about salaat said: \"For its votary, salaat shall on the Day of Judgement, be a light for him, an argument in his favour, and a means of his deliverance. Whereas there will be no light, no defence and no deliverance", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}], "pageNumber": 37}'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO temp_import_pages VALUES ('{"pageId": "c0380000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "bookPartId": "59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7", "sourceShowsPrintedPageLabel": true, "printedPageLabel": "38", "printedPageNumber": 38, "pdfPageNumber": 421, "sequenceIndex": 28, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "scanLanguages": ["en"], "reviewEvidence": {"englishTranscriptionComplete": true, "arabicTranscriptionComplete": false, "blockOrderChecked": true, "identifiersChecked": true, "scanCompared": true, "provenanceNotes": "Canonical transcription checked against the rendered secondary scan; master PDF page mapping retained. Fine vocalisation is preserved where clearly legible; no unresolved Arabic word or letter remains. English OCR correction and Arabic/translation-pair classification pass compared against the rendered source scan; raw OCR retained unchanged."}, "structuralNodes": [{"id": "a6000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "parentId": null, "nodeType": "section", "sourceLabel": "PART I", "sourceIdentifier": "I", "title": "IMPORTANCE OF SALAAT", "sequenceIndex": 0, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}, {"id": "a6100000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "parentId": "a6000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "nodeType": "chapter", "sourceLabel": "CHAPTER.—II", "sourceIdentifier": "II", "title": "WARNING AND REPROACH FOR NEGLECTING SALAAT", "sequenceIndex": 1, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}, {"id": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "parentId": "a6100000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "nodeType": "hadith", "sourceLabel": "Hadith VI", "sourceIdentifier": "VI", "title": null, "sequenceIndex": 2, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}], "blocks": [{"id": "d0380000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "from doom for him who does not guard his salaat, and he shall meet the fate of Pharoah, Haamaan and Ubbay bin'' Khalaf. \" Everybody knows that Pharoah—the big disbeliever— had been so arrogant that he proclaimed himself ''Lord the Highest'' and made his people worship him. Haamaan was his Chief Minister and accomplice. Ubbay bin Khalaf was the most active and severest enemy of Islam among the disbelievers of Mecaa. Before the Hijrah, he used to announce to the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) most insolently, \"I have reared a horse, which I feed very well; I will slay you one day riding on its back.\" Once the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) replied to him, ''Inshaa-allaah! you shall meet your end at my hands.\" In the battle of Uhud, he ran about in the field in search of the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"If Muhammad (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) is not slain today, then I stand no chance of surviving.\" He at last found the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) and advanced to attack him. The Companions decided to finish him before he reached the Prophet, but the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) stopped them. When he came near, the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) took a spear from one of the companions and struck him with it, causing a little scratch on his neck. He staggered and fell down from his horse and then fled towards his camp crying, \"By Allah, Muhammad (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) has killed me!\" His people tried to console him and told him that it was only a bruise and there was nothing to worry about, but he would say, \"Muhammad (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) had once announced to me in Mecca, that he would kill me. By Allah, had he only spat at me, I would be no more.\" It is said that he cried like a bull. Abu Sufyan, who was very active on that day, put him to shame for crying in that manner over a slight wound, but he said, \"Do you know who has inflicted this injury upon me? It was none other than Muhammad (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam). By Laat and Uzza! if my agony be distributed over all the people of Hijaaz, none of them would survive. Since the time he had declared that he would kill me, I was sure that I would meet my death at his hands. If he only spat at me after that declaration, I would be no more.\" So he died on his way back, at a day''s journey from Mecca. Look! a disbeliever like Ubbay bin Khalaf is so sure about the truth of the Prophet''s words that he does not", "rawOcrText": "38 Virtues of Salaat from doom for him who does not guard his salaat, and he shall meet the fate of Pharoah, Haamaan and Ubbay bin'' Khalaf. \" Everybody knows that Pharoah—the big disbeliever— had been so arrogant that he proclaimed himself ''Lord the Highest'' and made- his people worship him. Haamaan was his Chief Minister and accomplice. Ubbay bin Khalaf was the most active and severest enemy of Islam among the dis- believers of Mecaa. Before the Hijrah, he used to announce to the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) most insolently, \"I have reared a horse, which I feed very well; I will slay you one day riding on its back.\" Once the Prophet (Sallal- laho alaihe wasallam) replied to him, ''Clnshaa-allaah! you shall meet your end at my hands.\" In the battle of Uhud, he ran about in the field in search of the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"If Muhammad (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) is not slain today, then I stand no chance of sur- viving.\" He at last found the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wa- sallam) and advanced to attack him. The Com anions decided to finish him before he reached the Proplet, but the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) stopped them. When he came near, the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasal- lam) took a spear from one of the companions and struck him with it, causing a little scratch on his neck. He stag- gered and fell down from his horse and then fled towards his camp crying, \"By Allah, Muhammad (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) has killed me!\" His people tried to console him and told him that it was only a bruise and there was noth- ing to worry about, but he would say, \"Muhammad (Sallal- laho alaihe wasallam) had once announced to me in Meccq,- that he would kill me. By Allah, had he only spat at me,• I would be no more.\" It is said that he cried like a bull. Abu Sufyan, who was very active on that day, put him to shame for crying in that manner over a slight wound, but he said, \"Do you know who has inflicted this injury upon me? It was none other than Muhammad (Sallallaho alaihe wasal- lam). By Laat and Uzza! if my agony be distributed over all the people of Hijaaz, none of them would survive. Since the time •he had declared that he would kill me, I was sure that I would meet my death at his hands. If he only spat at me after that declaration, I would be no more.\" So he died on his way back, at a day''s journey from Mecca. Look! a disbeliever like Ubbay bin Khalaf is so sure about the outh of the Prophet''s words that he does not", "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}], "pageNumber": 38}'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO temp_import_pages VALUES ('{"pageId": "c0390000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "bookPartId": "59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7", "sourceShowsPrintedPageLabel": true, "printedPageLabel": "39", "printedPageNumber": 39, "pdfPageNumber": 422, "sequenceIndex": 29, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "scanLanguages": ["en", "ar"], "reviewEvidence": {"englishTranscriptionComplete": true, "arabicTranscriptionComplete": true, "blockOrderChecked": true, "identifiersChecked": true, "scanCompared": true, "provenanceNotes": "Canonical transcription checked against the rendered secondary scan; master PDF page mapping retained. Fine vocalisation is preserved where clearly legible; no unresolved Arabic word or letter remains. English OCR correction and Arabic/translation-pair classification pass compared against the rendered source scan; raw OCR retained unchanged."}, "structuralNodes": [{"id": "a6000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "parentId": null, "nodeType": "section", "sourceLabel": "PART I", "sourceIdentifier": "I", "title": "IMPORTANCE OF SALAAT", "sequenceIndex": 0, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}, {"id": "a6100000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "parentId": "a6000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "nodeType": "chapter", "sourceLabel": "CHAPTER.—II", "sourceIdentifier": "II", "title": "WARNING AND REPROACH FOR NEGLECTING SALAAT", "sequenceIndex": 1, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}, {"id": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007", "parentId": "a6100000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "nodeType": "hadith", "sourceLabel": "Hadith VII", "sourceIdentifier": "VII", "title": null, "sequenceIndex": 2, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}], "blocks": [{"id": "d0390000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007", "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "have the slightest doubt about his own death; but where do we stand? Although we believe in him as the greatest Prophet of Allah, consider his words to be most genuine and boast of our love for him, yet how far do we act upon his advice and how much do we fear the punishments about which he has warned us! It is for each one of us to ponder over and answer. Ibn Hajar, while quoting this hadith, has also mentioned Qaaroon with Pharaoh and others. He writes: \"Sharing the fate of these people on the Day of Judgement is due to the fact that it is often the pursuits specific to these guilty persons which cause neglect of salaat. If, therefore, a person neglects salaat due to a craving for wealth, he will meet the fate of Qaaroon; if due to love for power, then that of Pharaoh; if due to a yearning for attachment to a ruler, then that of Haamaan; and if due to occupation in trade then that of Ubbay Bin Khalaf.\" Meeting the same fate as theirs, explains fully the severest tortures in store for those who neglect salaat. Although the disbelievers shall have to suffer their doom forever, while the believers will be released after their period of punishment is over and will ultimately be allowed to enter Paradise, yet this period of punishment, who knows, may last for thousands of years.", "rawOcrText": "Part I (b)—Warning on Discard of Salaat 39 have the slightest doubt about his own death; but where do we stand? Although we believe .in him as the greatest Prophet •of Allah, consider his words to be most genuine and boast of our love for him, yet how far do we act upon his advice and how much do we fear the punishments about which he has warned us! It is for each one of us to ponder over and answer. Ibn Hajar, while quoting this hadith, has also men- tioned Qaaroon with Pharaoh and others. He writes: \"Shar- ing the fate of these people on the Day of Judgement is due to the fact that it is often the pursuits specific to these guilty persons which cause neglect of salaat. If, therefore, a person neglects salaat due to a craving for wealth, he. will meet the fate of Qaaroon; if due to love for power, then that of Pharaoh; if due to a yearning for attachment to a ruler, then that of Haamaan; and if due to occupation in trade then that of Ubbay Bin Khalaf.\" Meeting the same fate as theirs, explains fully the severest tortures in store for those who neglect salaat. Although the disbelievers shall have to suffer their doom forever, while the believers will be re- leased after their period of punishment is over and will ul- timately be allowed to enter Paradise, yet this period of punishment, who knows, may last for thousands of years. Hadith VII d) Gij ,", "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0390000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007", "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadith VII", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0390000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007", "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "قَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ وَرَدَ فِي الْحَدِيثِ أَنَّ مَنْ حَافَظَ عَلَى الصَّلَاةِ أَكْرَمَهُ اللَّهُ بِخَمْسِ خِصَالٍ يَرْفَعُ عَنْهُ ضِيقَ الْعَيْشِ وَعَذَابَ الْقَبْرِ وَيُعْطِيهِ اللَّهُ كِتَابَهُ بِيَمِينِهِ وَيَمُرُّ عَلَى الصِّرَاطِ كَالْبَرْقِ وَيَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ وَمَنْ تَهَاوَنَ عَنِ الصَّلَاةِ عَاقَبَهُ اللَّهُ بِخَمْسَ عَشْرَةَ عُقُوبَةً خَمْسَةٌ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَثَلَاثٌ عِنْدَ الْمَوْتِ وَثَلَاثٌ فِي قَبْرِهِ وَثَلَاثٌ عِنْدَ خُرُوجِهِ مِنَ الْقَبْرِ أَمَّا اللَّوَاتِي فِي الدُّنْيَا فَالْأُولَى تُنْزَعُ الْبَرَكَةُ مِنْ عُمُرِهِ وَالثَّانِيَةُ تُمْحَى سِيمَا الصَّالِحِينَ مِنْ وَجْهِهِ وَالثَّالِثَةُ كُلُّ عَمَلٍ يَعْمَلُهُ لَا يُؤَاجِرُهُ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَالرَّابِعَةُ لَا يُرْفَعُ لَهُ دُعَاءٌ إِلَى السَّمَاءِ وَالْخَامِسَةُ لَيْسَ لَهُ حَظٌّ فِي دُعَاءِ الصَّالِحِينَ وَأَمَّا الَّتِي تُصِيبُهُ عِنْدَ الْمَوْتِ فَإِنَّهُ يَمُوتُ ذَلِيلًا وَالثَّانِيَةُ يَمُوتُ جَوْعَانَ وَالثَّالِثَةُ يَمُوتُ عَطْشَانَ وَلَوْ سُقِيَ بِحَارَ الدُّنْيَا مَا رُوِيَ مِنْ عَطَشِهِ وَأَمَّا الَّتِي تُصِيبُهُ فِي قَبْرِهِ فَالْأُولَى يُضَيَّقُ عَلَيْهِ الْقَبْرُ حَتَّى تَخْتَلِفَ أَضْلَاعُهُ وَالثَّانِيَةُ يُوقَدُ عَلَيْهِ الْقَبْرُ نَارًا فَيَتَقَلَّبُ عَلَى الْجَمْرِ لَيْلًا وَنَهَارًا", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}], "pageNumber": 39}'::jsonb);
